This Ques has various approaches related to DP:
1. Recursion + Memoization (Using 2 pointers)
2. Recursion + Memoization (Using LCS concept where 2nd string the reverse of that string)
3. Bottom Up (Using LCS)
4. Bottom Up (normal dp[i][j] = LPS between i and j index)
5. Bottom Up (Using BluePrint)

1:
class Solution {
    int[][] t;
    private int solve(int i , int j , String s){
        if(i == j) return 1;

        if(i > j) return 0;

        if(t[i][j] != -1) return t[i][j];

        if(s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j)){
            return t[i][j] = 2 + solve(i+1 , j-1 , s);
        }

        int take_i = solve(i , j-1 , s);

        int take_j = solve(i+1 , j , s);


        return t[i][j] = Math.max(take_i , take_j);
    }
    public int longestPalindromeSubseq(String s) {
        int n = s.length();

        t = new int[n][n];
        for(int i = 0; i<n; i++){
            Arrays.fill(t[i] , -1);
        }

        return solve(0 , n-1 , s);
    }
}

T.C. -> O(n^2)
S.C. -> O(n^2) (Memoization Array) , Stack Memory (Recursion): O(n)

